    {
      "id": "y4I7cNj7kSOL9v9ukiG2F",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3373,
      "y": 2394,
      "width": 402.8797607421875,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1guV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2120566920,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1966179320,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245303738,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "grwbKind": "answer"
      },
      "text": "That's a real find, and it's bigger\nthan Friday. It's in, roles not names.\n\nNot knowing it could read that file\nis exactly why this needs an owner,\nand not just more care from each person.\nSame root, so I linked it there.\n\nI split your answer in two: the login\nbeing there, and nobody checking what\nthe agent could read.\n\n\"Only one login, and it can do\neverything\" has a ?. Inherited and\nkept for 2 years, so test it: if the\nagent could only have reached a login\nthat can't drop tables, would Friday\nstill have happened?\n\nThen the staging branch: why had\nthe staging login expired?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "That's a real find, and it's bigger\nthan Friday. It's in, roles not names.\n\nNot knowing it could read that file\nis exactly why this needs an owner,\nand not just more care from each person.\nSame root, so I linked it there.\n\nI split your answer in two: the login\nbeing there, and nobody checking what\nthe agent could read.\n\n\"Only one login, and it can do\neverything\" has a ?. Inherited and\nkept for 2 years, so test it: if the\nagent could only have reached a login\nthat can't drop tables, would Friday\nstill have happened?\n\nThen the staging branch: why had\nthe staging login expired?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "gUT1pWBFqlZN1KUWTptZy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3376.9398803710938,
      "y": 2964,
      "width": 1754.57861328125,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1gv",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 349750776,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1885270920,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245129141,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "no. if that login couldnt drop tables it just gets an error and stops. annoying but friday doesnt happen. ok so that one holds\nstaging login expires by itself every 90 days. theres no reminder. it dies, whoever trips over it resets it. it died on tuesday, nobody noticed bc nobody had used staging that week\nwhich is kind of embarrassing tbh\nI hate that its more us than it. still think it should have stopped and said something but ok",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "no. if that login couldnt drop tables it just gets an error and stops. annoying but friday doesnt happen. ok so that one holds\nstaging login expires by itself every 90 days. theres no reminder. it dies, whoever trips over it resets it. it died on tuesday, nobody noticed bc nobody had used staging that week\nwhich is kind of embarrassing tbh\nI hate that its more us than it. still think it should have stopped and said something but ok",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
