    },
    {
      "id": "fG4ElwC7ezUw43XoPHMyw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6065.28010559082,
      "y": 105,
      "width": 339.4397888183594,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1h0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2058678185,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 1372470919,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245303632,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "grwbKind": "claudeItem"
      },
      "text": "Root cause\nNo reminder warns the team before\nthe staging login expires.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "fw-a4",
      "originalText": "Root cause\nNo reminder warns the team before\nthe staging login expires.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xOBE7XKgLrKBR4BGqiQPh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3207,
      "y": 3076,
      "width": 391.7397766113281,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1h1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 462102633,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 872229705,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245157012,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "grwbKind": "answer"
      },
      "text": "Nothing to be embarrassed about. Most\nsmall teams have a login like that.\nIt's in, with a ? on the root.\n\nAbout \"more us than it\". Five Whys only\nkeeps what your team can change, so\nit will always look like that. It shows\nwhat's in your hands. It doesn't\nmeasure blame. The agent should have\nstopped and said something, and that's\nstill on the chart and still going to\nthe vendor. Both are true.\n\nThe one-login root holds, by your test.\nI took the ? off.\n\nOne branch left: why did the agent not\ntell the engineer it had switched?\nIf the answer sits with the vendor,\nwhat on your side could have caught it?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Nothing to be embarrassed about. Most\nsmall teams have a login like that.\nIt's in, with a ? on the root.\n\nAbout \"more us than it\". Five Whys only\nkeeps what your team can change, so\nit will always look like that. It shows\nwhat's in your hands. It doesn't\nmeasure blame. The agent should have\nstopped and said something, and that's\nstill on the chart and still going to\nthe vendor. Both are true.\n\nThe one-login root holds, by your test.\nI took the ? off.\n\nOne branch left: why did the agent not\ntell the engineer it had switched?\nIf the answer sits with the vendor,\nwhat on your side could have caught it?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "y4wuxn4idwvto5JNxbdfx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3205.369888305664,
      "y": 3631,
      "width": 1857.3385009765625,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1h3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 952643576,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 433957256,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245180530,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "our side: the whole answer was in the log and I only read the \"all done\" bit. I always do, the log is miles long\nnothing on the db tells anyone when a table goes. first I knew was customers getting errors\nand we never told it to say which database it used. the notes file could say that I guess, but after this I dont fully trust it to obey a note. so a note AND something it cant get around?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "our side: the whole answer was in the log and I only read the \"all done\" bit. I always do, the log is miles long\nnothing on the db tells anyone when a table goes. first I knew was customers getting errors\nand we never told it to say which database it used. the notes file could say that I guess, but after this I dont fully trust it to obey a note. so a note AND something it cant get around?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
