      "text": "Why 2\nThe team never told the agent\nto say which database it used.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "fw-o2b",
      "originalText": "Why 2\nThe team never told the agent\nto say which database it used.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uWKgvIvnCflHUPuHT42uh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5450.000091552734,
      "y": 617.5,
      "width": 369.99981689453125,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1hD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1863907657,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 961814823,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245303632,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "grwbKind": "claudeItem"
      },
      "text": "Root cause\nNo one owns how the agent is set up.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "fw-o3b",
      "originalText": "Root cause\nNo one owns how the agent is set up.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5F2hOX0AwHWflgUpKPMab",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5566.410095214844,
      "y": 705,
      "width": 367.1798095703125,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1hE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 629607337,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 855168999,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245303632,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "grwbKind": "claudeItem"
      },
      "text": "Outflow, Root cause\nNothing on the database tells anyone\nwhen a table goes.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "fw-o1c",
      "originalText": "Outflow, Root cause\nNothing on the database tells anyone\nwhen a table goes.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uhyZfvIIXaU59bEthciNu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3035,
      "y": 4270,
      "width": 414.9797668457031,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1hH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 726293193,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1353062825,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245225965,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "grwbKind": "answer"
      },
      "text": "Yes. A note AND something it can't\nget around. You said it better than I\ncould: a note asks, a limit doesn't\nneed to.\n\nAll on the chart now. \"Log is miles\nlong\" has a ?. Nobody will read miles\nof log, so I'd let it go and let the\nother boxes do that job. Your call.\n\nThe whys are done. These are your roots:\n1. No one owns how the agent is set up.\n2. Only one production login exists,\n   and it can do everything.\n3. No reminder warns the team before\n   the staging login expires.\n4. Nothing on the database tells\n   anyone when a table goes.\n\nDo 1, 3 and 4 hold as roots for you?\n\nIf they do, give me one sentence for\neach: what you'll do about it, and\nwhich role owns it.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Yes. A note AND something it can't\nget around. You said it better than I\ncould: a note asks, a limit doesn't\nneed to.\n\nAll on the chart now. \"Log is miles\nlong\" has a ?. Nobody will read miles\nof log, so I'd let it go and let the\nother boxes do that job. Your call.\n\nThe whys are done. These are your roots:\n1. No one owns how the agent is set up.\n2. Only one production login exists,\n   and it can do everything.\n3. No reminder warns the team before\n   the staging login expires.\n4. Nothing on the database tells\n   anyone when a table goes.\n\nDo 1, 3 and 4 hold as roots for you?\n\nIf they do, give me one sentence for\neach: what you'll do about it, and\nwhich role owns it.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "v1RKWxHQXfbQ3k-0js1G9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3034.9898834228516,
      "y": 4922.5,
      "width": 1684.4591064453125,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1hJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2118312840,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1792350968,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245249739,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "yes they hold. log gone, fine\n1. founder names one owner, one shared agent setup for all laptops, finer permissions, no whole session allow. owner: backend lead (me I guess)\n2. separate logins: app, read only for people + agents, write login only out of password manager when 2 people are looking. no prod logins in local config. owner: backend lead\n3. shared calendar reminder 2 wks before staging login dies, reset it then. owner: support lead\n4. alert to the team when a table gets dropped. owner: backend lead\nthats 3 of 4 on me, thats not great\nalso nobody had ever tried a restore + point in time was off. why isnt that on the chart? we got lucky",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "yes they hold. log gone, fine\n1. founder names one owner, one shared agent setup for all laptops, finer permissions, no whole session allow. owner: backend lead (me I guess)\n2. separate logins: app, read only for people + agents, write login only out of password manager when 2 people are looking. no prod logins in local config. owner: backend lead\n3. shared calendar reminder 2 wks before staging login dies, reset it then. owner: support lead\n4. alert to the team when a table gets dropped. owner: backend lead\nthats 3 of 4 on me, thats not great\nalso nobody had ever tried a restore + point in time was off. why isnt that on the chart? we got lucky",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
