      "updated": 1794245303770,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "grwbKind": "claudeItem"
      },
      "text": "Why 2\nNobody had ever tried a restore.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "fw-r2b",
      "originalText": "Why 2\nNobody had ever tried a restore.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "S66c1vbNr8vPA0QIed4JM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2865,
      "y": 5110,
      "width": 387.53973388671875,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1hT",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 235837831,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 540004519,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245303987,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "grwbKind": "answer"
      },
      "text": "Good catch, and that one's on me.\nI wrote the problem as \"dropped the\ntables\", which left out why it cost\nyou a whole clinic day. It's a third\nbranch now, Recovery. And yes, you got\nlucky. The chart should say so.\n\nYour 4 measures are in. They remove\ntheir roots. One check on 1: the shared\nsetup also needs your note (stop and\nask, say which database), or two boxes\non that branch stay open. In?\n\n3 of 4 on you is worth saying out loud\nto your founder on Monday. An owner\nwith no time is no owner, and that's\nroot 1 again.\n\nRecovery, Why 3.\nWhy was point in time off, and why had\nnobody ever tried a restore?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Good catch, and that one's on me.\nI wrote the problem as \"dropped the\ntables\", which left out why it cost\nyou a whole clinic day. It's a third\nbranch now, Recovery. And yes, you got\nlucky. The chart should say so.\n\nYour 4 measures are in. They remove\ntheir roots. One check on 1: the shared\nsetup also needs your note (stop and\nask, say which database), or two boxes\non that branch stay open. In?\n\n3 of 4 on you is worth saying out loud\nto your founder on Monday. An owner\nwith no time is no owner, and that's\nroot 1 again.\n\nRecovery, Why 3.\nWhy was point in time off, and why had\nnobody ever tried a restore?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "PJwg3ck_-mvtjyx89aZv5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2861.2698669433594,
      "y": 5692.5,
      "width": 1531.4990234375,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1hU",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 584619400,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1021839608,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794245324347,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "yes note in. ok will tell her monday, Jonah could take the alert maybe\npoint in time: it costs extra and the cheap plan doesnt turn it on. the guy who left picked that, no handover, I dont think anyone knew it was a choice\nnever tried a restore bc its nobody's job. backups just had a green tick on a page so we assumed\nsame thing as root 1 really, nobody owns it. turn point in time on monday, and a practice restore every 3 months, founder owns that one so its not me again",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "yes note in. ok will tell her monday, Jonah could take the alert maybe\npoint in time: it costs extra and the cheap plan doesnt turn it on. the guy who left picked that, no handover, I dont think anyone knew it was a choice\nnever tried a restore bc its nobody's job. backups just had a green tick on a page so we assumed\nsame thing as root 1 really, nobody owns it. turn point in time on monday, and a practice restore every 3 months, founder owns that one so its not me again",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
